@startuml elevated_broker_architecture
!include ../btadn/dark-theme.puml
' Added 2026-09-28; revised 2026-09-29: six ops wired through the broker, terminate still separate (deferred)
title Elevated privileged-action broker - lazy per-action consent, six ops wired, terminate deferred

legend top right
  |= color |= zone |
  |<$TINT_BLUE>| Medium integrity (asInvoker) |
  |<$TINT_AMBER>| Elevated (consented on demand) |
  |<$TINT_NEUTRAL>| Windows admin surfaces |
endlegend

package "Medium integrity  (asInvoker - the normal tray app)" $TINT_BLUE {
  [Action call sites\nProcessRowContextMenu: priority / affinity / dump\nServicesPage: start / stop / restart / disable\nStartupAppsPage: enable / disable (all-users)\nUsersPage: disconnect another session] as CALLERS
  component "ElevatedActionCoordinator\nAppServices.ElevatedActions\n(single entry; owns consent)" as COORD
  [ProcessTerminationService\n(standard helper + managed handle;\nend task stays on this path)] as PTS
  component "Settings\nEnableElevatedTerminationOnStartup (default off)\nBypassElevationBrokerWhenElevated (default off)" as SETTINGS
}

package "Elevated  (consented per action until granted, then reused)" $TINT_AMBER {
  component "ElevationBroker\ntmtadn.exe --elevated-broker\nSetPriority / SetAffinity / CreateDump /\nServiceControl / SetStartupApproval / DisconnectSession" as BROKER
  component "Native kill helper\ntmtadn.exe --kill-helper (or KillHelper.exe)\nterminate only; NOT via the broker yet" as KH
}

package "Windows administrative surfaces" $TINT_NEUTRAL {
  [SCM (advapi32)] as SCM
  [HKLM StartupApproved\n(registry)] as HKLM
  [Session control (WTS)] as WTS
  [Process handles\n(priority / affinity / dump / terminate)] as PROC
}

CALLERS --> COORD : escalate when the in-process\nattempt is denied (or all-users startup)
COORD --> BROKER : named-pipe request\n[current-user ACL + client image check]
COORD ..> PROC : direct in-process\n(only when elevated + bypass setting)
BROKER --> SCM : start / stop / restart / disable
BROKER --> HKLM : all-users startup toggle
BROKER --> WTS : disconnect session
BROKER --> PROC : set priority / affinity / create dump
PTS --> KH : arm / fire over shared memory
KH --> PROC : OpenProcess(PROCESS_TERMINATE)\n+ TerminateProcess
SETTINGS ..> COORD
SETTINGS ..> KH

note right of COORD $TINT_BLUE
  Lazy per-action consent (no eager prompt):
  1. The op runs in-process at medium IL; on ACCESS_DENIED
     (or a deterministic all-users startup entry) it escalates.
  2. The UI shows an in-app confirmation, then ShellExecute "runas"
     launches the broker: one Windows UAC prompt.
  3. A decline changes nothing and is NOT remembered - every later
     admin action prompts again until elevation is actually granted.
  4. Once the broker is up it is reused for the session with no
     further prompts.
end note

note bottom of BROKER $TINT_AMBER
  Security model (the one elevated surface):
  - Pipe ACL restricted to the current user.
  - Broker verifies the connecting client is this executable's
    image before serving any request.
  - Only the fixed op set above is accepted; no arbitrary-exec.
end note

note bottom of KH $TINT_NEUTRAL
  Process termination still uses the existing kill helper, not the
  broker. Its elevated startup attempt is now gated by the
  EnableElevatedTerminationOnStartup setting (default off), so there
  is no eager UAC prompt. Unifying terminate under the broker (and
  spawning the kill helper from it) remains the deferred next step.
end note

@enduml
